                <pb facs="0249" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10388.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon refers to department’s telegraphic instruction of June 8, 1906, and
                    instructs Mr. Rockhill to report whether the claims of American citizens have
                    been carefully substantiated, and to forward them to department for
                    approval.)</p>
            </div>
